<title>USA: CCC seeks 85,000 T corn for Aug/Sep for N. Korea.</title>
<headline>CCC seeks 85,000 T corn for Aug/Sep for N. Korea.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commodity Credit Corp (CCC) said it is seeking up to 85,000 tonnes of U.S. corn for shipment between August 1 and September 10 to North Korea.</p>
<p>CCC seeks Number 2 or better yellow corn, 14.5 percent maximum moisture, under Title II funding of the Agency for International Development (AID).</p>
<p>An AID spokeswoman said on July 14 that the United States would donate corn and rice to aid North Korea, which is suffering from a famine.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel, Chicago newsdesk, 312 408 8720))</p>
